                    {
                        "form_id": "84760154-2540-4c29-b04c-4bbc8b88623a",
                        "entry_id": "1888ea0a-43a1-33d9-ada8-8c73f496d738",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "prepositional"
                        ],
                        "form": "ре́дьках"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "55eeacb7-10e9-323f-b4e8-1ee65f83d79f",
                        "entry_id": "1888ea0a-43a1-33d9-ada8-8c73f496d738",
                        "glosses": [
                            "ботан. двухлетнее травянистое растение из семейства крестоцветных с плодом в виде стручка и корнеплодом, обладающим характерным горьким вкусом"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d5d7c011-45dc-33ce-a703-2e36afbfee18",
                        "entry_id": "1888ea0a-43a1-33d9-ada8-8c73f496d738",
                        "glosses": [
                            "кулин. корнеплод этого растения, употребляемый в пищу"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6d5197ab-1eca-4eb5-aa9e-3bfe41f4af0f",
                                "sense_id": "d5d7c011-45dc-33ce-a703-2e36afbfee18",
                                "text": ".. под забором Стёпушка сидит и редьку гложет .."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4238b5ff-57c0-4f6f-bed5-28be71a7e500",
                                "sense_id": "d5d7c011-45dc-33ce-a703-2e36afbfee18",
                                "text": "— А что, два фунта патоки съешь? — Съем. — А четыре миски каши? — Съем... — А пять редек?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d468258f-98f2-43cc-9cc4-e3f44255efb1",
                                "sense_id": "d5d7c011-45dc-33ce-a703-2e36afbfee18",
                                "text": "Будучи гурманом и пресытившись тонкостями иностранной кухни, обжираясь паштетами, трюфелями и ананасами, он иногда чувствовал неодолимую потребность поесть солёных огурцов, редьки, клюквы, капусты."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c3c58ae0-8b60-499e-bb57-0129194e3ac1",
                                "sense_id": "d5d7c011-45dc-33ce-a703-2e36afbfee18",
                                "text": ".. на этот раз на столе были цвет и краса нашей кухни: рубленая селёдка, тёртая редька, печёночный паштет, фаршированная рыба .."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "007bab45-03c3-4f29-9887-5e9bd992e3bd",
                        "source_entry_id": "1888ea0a-43a1-33d9-ada8-8c73f496d738",
                        "source_sense_description": "двухлетнее травянистое растение",
                        "target_lang_word": "radish",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "radish",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "639c2bd1-b55a-3a6d-865b-fde4e6da69d1",
                                        "entry_id": "1237e91c-8870-326c-b40a-9a58488de452",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A plant of the Brassicaceae family, Raphanus sativus or Raphanus raphanistrum subsp. sativus, having an edible root."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4c397cb3-86b9-4c5b-a354-059880cb123f",
                                                "sense_id": "639c2bd1-b55a-3a6d-865b-fde4e6da69d1",
                                                "text": "Many times they ſow divers ſeeds in a Bed together, as Radiſhes and Carrots, that by ſuch time as the Carrots come up, the Radiſhes may be gone. Upon beds newly ſet with Licorice they ſow Onions or Radiſh, or Lettice if their Licorice plants or ground be but weak, ſo as not quickly to cauſe a ſhadow with their leaves."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "370671fc-2a38-40bd-ad2f-54d2a693fdcf",
                                                "sense_id": "639c2bd1-b55a-3a6d-865b-fde4e6da69d1",
                                                "text": "The newly-introduced radish, which has attracted the attention of horticulturists so much of late, is certainly a novelty, inasmuch as the edible portion of the plant is the seed-vessel, and not the root. The common radish, in its numerous varieties, in such an exceedingly popular salad-plant, that we are scarcely prepared to look to this genus for new economic products or floral novelties. When we consider the many varieties of radish known to this country, from the long and tapering red-root to the white turnip-radish, we might, in some measure, be prepared for a wider development of nature's laws in tropical countries."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1010497e-9d3b-4cc5-8661-9b3407323d72",
                                                "sense_id": "639c2bd1-b55a-3a6d-865b-fde4e6da69d1",
                                                "text": "Although hardly coming under my theme, I cannot omit this: \"Against a woman's chatter: Taste at night fasting a root of radish, that day the chatter cannot harm thee.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "220442d9-e12b-33d5-b4a1-1226d5777d0c",
                                        "entry_id": "1237e91c-8870-326c-b40a-9a58488de452",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The root of this plant used as food. Some varieties are pungent and usually eaten raw in salads, etc., while others have a milder taste and are cooked."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "91b09953-5c81-4ed0-95c0-0421d795937b",
                                                "sense_id": "220442d9-e12b-33d5-b4a1-1226d5777d0c",
                                                "text": "Fat people ſhould not eat freely of oily, nouriſhing diet. They ought frequently to eat radiſh, garlic, ſpices, or ſuch things as are heating, and promote perſpiration and urine."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0d24e0b5-ca10-42c6-9c6e-6597f39c8c6e",
                                                "sense_id": "220442d9-e12b-33d5-b4a1-1226d5777d0c",
                                                "text": "The flavors of radicchio and radish are delicious with only a touch of balsamic vinegar for a dressing."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b21199b2-89a8-4e45-ac22-fa7549a7d8aa",
                                                "sense_id": "220442d9-e12b-33d5-b4a1-1226d5777d0c",
                                                "text": "Purple shoots had grown up from the wheat seeds sown in the furrows. He fell to his knees and dug up a radish. There was a sound like a bubble popping as the thin roots parted from the earth."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c8e98016-57a2-353a-af9f-b97b73a195f6",
                                        "entry_id": "1237e91c-8870-326c-b40a-9a58488de452",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Some other root plant of genus Raphanus or family Brassicaceae."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "in-compounds",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "57a3d066-691b-47f8-ba95-62a58e4c0502",
                                                "sense_id": "c8e98016-57a2-353a-af9f-b97b73a195f6",
                                                "text": "rat-tail radish (Raphanus caudatus); wild radish (Raphanus raphanistrum)"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "51665dd3-4aa4-42bd-a998-7c1f2853b198",
                                                "sense_id": "c8e98016-57a2-353a-af9f-b97b73a195f6",
                                                "text": "The Wild Radish (Raphanus raphanistrum), is Edward's trophy, brought from a piece of waste ground near Hawkhurst, in Kent. The petals are white or pale lilac, veined distinctly with a deeper shade. The Sea Radish (R. maritimus,[…]), is primrose-coloured, also veined. Fanny brought it from the beautiful cliffs near Lizard Point."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4fed69e8-4392-4d94-8064-2de35fab9c3d",
                                                "sense_id": "c8e98016-57a2-353a-af9f-b97b73a195f6",
                                                "text": "Radishes were something new for me. The first time I tried growing for seed, I was surprised by the shape of the pods; they looked like hot peppers. Being the curious type I nibbled on a few pods and found they were delicious when still in the immature stage. I thought I had discovered something novel when, lo and behold, I found out that radishes grown in India just for their pods—a variety called Rat-Tail radish—for many years."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
